WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:06.960 --> 00:00:10.860
[Narrator:] The patient with multiple sclerosis
staggers down a long road,

00:00:11.340 --> 00:00:14.940
weaving between despair on the one side and
hope on the other.

00:00:15.600 --> 00:00:21.080
The doctor who must guide this patient is
faced with a disorder in which the diagnosis

00:00:21.080 --> 00:00:23.560
is a gamble of odds and probabilities.

00:00:24.080 --> 00:00:30.700
The etiology is hidden in a jungle of clues
and the therapy stirs a broth of heated dispute.

00:00:31.180 --> 00:00:37.780
It is hoped that this film will enable the
practitioner and the student to better understand

00:00:37.880 --> 00:00:39.320
this elusive disease.

00:00:40.300 --> 00:00:55.080
[Music]

00:00:55.240 --> 00:01:00.920
[Narrator:] This is a...at 19, she had a two-week
episode of burning and hypersensitivity

00:01:00.920 --> 00:01:01.980
of the right arm.

00:01:02.440 --> 00:01:08.720
A second episode occurred nine months later,
beginning with sharp pains in the right forehead

00:01:08.720 --> 00:01:14.400
and scalp, then numbness and tingling in the right fingers and toes, ascending in three days

00:01:14.920 --> 00:01:17.960
to include the entire right side below the
neck.

00:01:18.220 --> 00:01:23.320
After one month, these symptoms had almost
cleared, but she then developed loss of vision

00:01:23.540 --> 00:01:29.240
in the left eye over a three-day period, followed
in two weeks by blurring of vision

00:01:29.240 --> 00:01:29.940
in the right eye

00:01:29.940 --> 00:01:32.320
with pain on movement of the eyes.

00:01:32.620 --> 00:01:38.400
At this time, she also noted a tingling down
the back, on bending the head forward.

00:01:39.260 --> 00:01:44.060
On examination at the peak of this attack,
she could only count fingers with the left eye,

00:01:45.360 --> 00:01:50.780
and the visual field showed a huge scotoma
involving the central region and the area

00:01:51.020 --> 00:01:52.840
around the blind spot.

00:01:53.180 --> 00:01:59.840
On the right, visual acuity was 20 over 40
and field-testing showed a scotoma involving the area

00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:06.880
around the blind spot and the entire inferior
nasal quadrant, but sparing central vision.

00:02:07.240 --> 00:02:09.580
The optic discs appeared normal.

00:02:10.020 --> 00:02:15.600
These findings of optic neuritis gradually
disappeared over the next two months.

00:02:15.860 --> 00:02:22.340
In the four years since then, she has remained
well, except for one persistent symptom.

00:02:23.080 --> 00:02:28.480
[Patient:] When I bend my neck down, I get
an electric shock sensation that extends

00:02:28.480 --> 00:02:32.060
from my neck down my back, through my legs.

00:02:32.560 --> 00:02:40.100
[Narrator:] This electric shock-like sensation on flexion of the neck is called Lhermitte's sign

00:02:40.480 --> 00:02:46.580
and is considered a manifestation of posterior
column damage in the cervical spinal cord.

00:02:48.380 --> 00:02:52.640
This is a 43-year-old sales manager for a
dairy company.

00:02:52.660 --> 00:02:59.260
At 33, he had an episode of left-sided numbness
and weakness, unsteady walk, and double vision,

00:02:59.260 --> 00:03:02.000
with complete recovery in six months.

00:03:02.140 --> 00:03:09.940
At 36, he developed slurred speech, difficulty focusing his eyes, clumsiness of the left arm and leg,

00:03:10.160 --> 00:03:15.460
hypersensitivity of the right side of the
body, and Lhermitte's sign.

00:03:15.760 --> 00:03:19.500
He improved after one month but was left with
permanent residual.

00:03:20.020 --> 00:03:23.980
This stayed the same for the next four years,
then slowly worsened.

00:03:24.180 --> 00:03:27.600
Ten years after onset, he demonstrates the
following:

00:03:28.680 --> 00:03:32.180
His eye movements are impaired in all directions
of gaze.

00:03:32.380 --> 00:03:35.740
When he looks to the sides, the in-turning
eye is paralyzed.

00:03:35.800 --> 00:03:38.940
The out-turning eye shows horizontal nystagmus.

00:03:39.200 --> 00:03:44.840
There is weakness of upward gaze, left more
than right, and vertical nystagmus

00:03:44.840 --> 00:03:47.520
on upward and downward gaze.

00:03:48.460 --> 00:03:54.360
This disconjugate gaze difficulty is called
internuclear ophthalmoplegia.

00:03:54.780 --> 00:04:00.400
It represents damage to the median longitudinal
fasciculus, a tract that runs through

00:04:00.600 --> 00:04:04.640
the dorsal portion of the brain stem on each
side of the midline.

00:04:05.080 --> 00:04:09.700
Bilateral internuclear ophthalmoplegia is
considered by many authorities

00:04:09.840 --> 00:04:13.160
to be pathognomonic of multiple sclerosis.

00:04:14.480 --> 00:04:20.220
His speech shows dysarthria characterized
by jerky rhythm and slurring.

00:04:21.120 --> 00:04:28.700
[Patient 2:] On July 24th, 1858, after consulting
friends about the proposal, Abraham Lincoln,

00:04:29.280 --> 00:04:38.140
the Republican candidate for senator, challenged
his Democratic opponent, the incumbent,

00:04:38.140 --> 00:04:46.620
Stephen A. Douglas, to divide time and address
the same audience during the present canva....

00:04:48.640 --> 00:04:53.240
[Narrator:] Testing of his hands shows good
coordination on the right.

00:04:53.760 --> 00:04:58.080
But on the left, there is a tremor of the
outstretched hand accentuated

00:04:58.080 --> 00:05:00.680
by performing any accuracy test.

00:05:00.940 --> 00:05:06.040
There is also inability to perform rapid alternating
movements with this hand.

00:05:06.260 --> 00:05:11.100
These signs represent the ataxia of cerebellar
disease.

00:05:12.520 --> 00:05:16.740
Testing of his legs reveals the weakness on
the left.

00:05:17.120 --> 00:05:33.840
[The doctor examines the way each leg reacts
to stretches.]

00:05:35.480 --> 00:05:38.040
There is ankle clonus on the left.

00:05:40.460 --> 00:05:45.060
There are bilateral upgoing toes on plantar
stimulation.

00:05:45.620 --> 00:05:50.580
These signs are indicative of damage to the
pyramidal tract somewhere between

00:05:50.780 --> 00:05:54.520
the cerebral cortex and the lumbar cord.

00:05:57.580 --> 00:06:00.960
This is a 23-year-old insurance company clerk.

00:06:01.200 --> 00:06:04.700
Beginning at age 18, she has had one episode
each year.

00:06:05.080 --> 00:06:09.580
The first attack consisted of buzzing and
decreased hearing in the left ear, double vision

00:06:10.280 --> 00:06:13.940
and impaired balance, with complete recovery
in six weeks.

00:06:14.160 --> 00:06:20.180
The second attack included left-sided tinnitus and hearing loss, staggering walk, double vision,

00:06:20.780 --> 00:06:26.120
slurred speech, tingling in the right hand,
and numbness in both legs below the knees.

00:06:26.280 --> 00:06:32.420
After six months, these symptoms improved, but she was left with permanent nystagmus and ataxia.

00:06:34.300 --> 00:06:40.260
Her third attack began with pain and foggy
vision in the right eye, reaching a peak in one month

00:06:40.320 --> 00:06:46.700
at which time the visual acuity was 20 over
30, and the visual fields showed a scotoma adjacent

00:06:46.800 --> 00:06:48.100
to the macular region.

00:06:48.560 --> 00:06:53.940
This paracentral scotoma of optic neuritis
remitted in another month.

00:06:55.520 --> 00:07:01.640
A right oculomotor nerve palsy lasting five
weeks constituted the fourth attack.

00:07:01.640 --> 00:07:07.080
She is now in her fifth attack with symptoms
of vertigo, slurred speech, double vision,

00:07:07.080 --> 00:07:09.840
staggering gait, and numbness in the right
hand.

00:07:11.680 --> 00:07:16.900
Examination of eye movements reveals coarse
horizontal nystagmus on lateral gaze,

00:07:17.060 --> 00:07:19.700
vertical nystagmus on gaze up and down.

00:07:20.160 --> 00:07:22.840
A rhythmic head tremor may also be seen.

00:07:23.040 --> 00:07:26.920
This represents damage to vestibular pathways.

00:07:28.160 --> 00:07:32.320
When she holds out the left hand, there is
a flapping tremor at the wrist,

00:07:32.320 --> 00:07:35.860
intensified by performance of the finger-to-nose
test.

00:07:36.000 --> 00:07:39.260
This is independent of whether the eyes are
open or closed.

00:07:39.480 --> 00:07:43.440
It represents the intention tremor of cerebellar
disease.

00:07:46.020 --> 00:07:50.880
The right hand exhibits searching movements
of the fingers when the eyes are closed,

00:07:51.140 --> 00:07:56.620
and hesitancy on the finger-to-nose test,
which is not present when the eyes are open,

00:07:56.620 --> 00:08:02.400
indicating position sense loss due to posterior
column damage in the spinal cord.

00:08:03.740 --> 00:08:08.420
Her gait is weaving and lurching because of
ataxia in the legs.

00:08:11.620 --> 00:08:14.400
She has bilateral ankle clonus.

00:08:19.020 --> 00:08:24.500
And Babinski signs as a result of pyramidal
tract damage.

00:08:30.840 --> 00:08:36.380
This is a 41-year-old housewife and mother
whose first symptoms occurred at age 30,

00:08:36.380 --> 00:08:38.780
when she developed weakness of the left leg.

00:08:39.460 --> 00:08:43.380
At 33, she had nystagmus and an ataxic gait.

00:08:43.640 --> 00:08:48.140
Since 35, both legs have become progressively
weaker and stiffer.

00:08:48.220 --> 00:08:49.820
There have been no remissions.

00:08:49.820 --> 00:08:52.760
After 11 years, she shows the following.

00:08:53.160 --> 00:08:58.160
Testing of eye movements demonstrates bilateral
internuclear ophthalmoplegia,

00:08:58.580 --> 00:09:04.620
with weakness of the adducting eye and jerking
of the abducting eye on gaze to each side.

00:09:10.660 --> 00:09:17.060
There is a mild intention tremor of both hands,
representing damage to the cerebellar system.

00:09:23.200 --> 00:09:26.240
Babinski signs are present bilaterally.

00:09:35.800 --> 00:09:41.100
Both legs show spasticity and weakness, the
left more than the right.

00:10:01.280 --> 00:10:04.660
The patellar reflexes are hyperactive bilaterally.

00:10:05.180 --> 00:10:11.700
This spastic paraparesis with hyperactive
and pathological reflexes denotes pyramidal

00:10:11.860 --> 00:10:14.460
tract damage in the spinal cord.

00:10:15.760 --> 00:10:20.800
This is a 41-year-old schoolteacher whose
symptoms began at age 31 when he developed

00:10:20.980 --> 00:10:26.800
difficulty focusing his eyes with apparent
movement of objects upon which he would fix.

00:10:27.080 --> 00:10:28.780
This represented nystagmus.

00:10:29.540 --> 00:10:32.380
It occurred intermittently for one year, then
disappeared.

00:10:32.780 --> 00:10:37.380
At 33, he noted intermittent balance difficulty
and weakness of the legs.

00:10:37.800 --> 00:10:40.880
At 34, incoordination of the hands and feet.

00:10:41.320 --> 00:10:46.040
At 36, his left leg and arm became weak and
have remained so ever since.

00:10:46.040 --> 00:10:48.640
After ten years, he shows the following.

00:10:49.520 --> 00:10:54.020
There is mild ataxia of all four limbs on
coordination testing.

00:10:54.140 --> 00:10:56.080
This is more prominent on the left.

00:10:56.300 --> 00:10:59.780
A slight head tremor occurs intermittently
with effort.

00:11:33.740 --> 00:11:37.500
Spasticity in the left arm and leg is demonstrated
when he walks.

00:11:37.800 --> 00:11:41.920
The left arm does not swing, and the left
leg is used stiffly.

00:11:42.280 --> 00:11:55.340
[The patient walks around to demostrate the
difference in the way each leg works.]

00:11:56.180 --> 00:11:59.360
The reflexes are hyperactive everywhere.

00:11:59.920 --> 00:12:25.220
[The patient's reflexes are tested in various
parts of his body.]

00:12:25.720 --> 00:12:28.580
Hoffmann signs are present bilaterally.

00:12:34.880 --> 00:12:38.080
There are bilateral Babinski signs.

00:12:38.320 --> 00:12:44.400
This patient's findings indicate damage to
the pyramidal tract and the cerebellar system

00:12:44.820 --> 00:12:48.820
bilaterally, most likely in the brain stem.

00:12:49.640 --> 00:12:53.660
Multiple sclerosis can be diagnosed with certainty
only at autopsy

00:12:53.700 --> 00:12:58.700
when a picture of patchy demyelination in
the central nervous system is seen.

00:13:00.280 --> 00:13:05.600
The glial scars or plaques may be seen and
felt on the surface of the brain or spinal cord,

00:13:06.440 --> 00:13:10.200
as grayish-brown, firm, translucent spots.

00:13:11.760 --> 00:13:17.320
All of these pictures are from one patient,
a 24-year-old lady with a four-year history

00:13:17.560 --> 00:13:19.060
of multiple sclerosis.

00:13:19.520 --> 00:13:26.560
Here on the pons is a large, brown, sclerotic
plaque with two smaller lesions above it.

00:13:28.180 --> 00:13:34.300
These lesions represent a late stage in the
pathological process, the demyelinated patch

00:13:34.600 --> 00:13:39.420
having been filled in by a scar of glial cell
overgrowth.

00:13:40.880 --> 00:13:47.360
When cut sections of brain or cord are viewed,
foci of demyelination appear as brown patches

00:13:47.500 --> 00:13:48.920
in the white matter.

00:13:50.520 --> 00:13:56.200
Cerebral foci have a predilection for the
white matter immediately adjacent to the ventricles,

00:13:56.420 --> 00:13:59.520
especially posterior and inferior horns,

00:14:00.620 --> 00:14:05.640
and the white matter about the cortical and
basal nuclear gray matter.

00:14:05.820 --> 00:14:10.300
The lesions in the cerebral hemisphere vary
in size from that of a pinhead

00:14:10.400 --> 00:14:13.380
to several centimeters in diameter.

00:14:14.680 --> 00:14:20.520
Similarly, numerous areas of discoloration
are found in the brain stem and cerebellum.

00:14:21.240 --> 00:14:25.260
Early in the plaque formation, there is perivascular
inflammation.

00:14:25.660 --> 00:14:29.180
Then tissue is destroyed, myelin preponderantly.

00:14:29.180 --> 00:14:36.340
Myelin sheaths fragment into globules, fat
is liberated, and macrophages ingest the fat.

00:14:37.500 --> 00:14:45.680
As the lesion ages, glial cells proliferate
and produce fibrils, which give the older lesions.

00:14:45.880 --> 00:14:50.780
their sclerotic appearance and make them visible
to the naked eye.

00:14:51.980 --> 00:14:56.940
Here on a freshly cut section of the spinal
cord, only a faint area of discoloration is seen

00:14:57.440 --> 00:14:58.960
in the posterior columns.

00:15:00.700 --> 00:15:06.600
When stained for myelin, the lesions appear as pale foci within the darkly staining white matter.

00:15:07.240 --> 00:15:09.940
Many more plaques are now apparent.

00:15:11.460 --> 00:15:15.220
The lesions are often far in excess of what
one would've expected

00:15:15.320 --> 00:15:18.700
from the patient's symptoms and signs during
life.

00:15:19.440 --> 00:15:24.320
Thus, many plaques may be clinically silent,
such as this demyelinated patch

00:15:24.320 --> 00:15:27.140
in the optic radiation of the cerebrum.

00:15:28.440 --> 00:15:33.120
In fact, there is evidence that a patient
may go through life with pathological demyelination

00:15:33.120 --> 00:15:37.240
and yet have no clinical manifestations of
multiple sclerosis.

00:15:39.060 --> 00:15:44.500
[Louis J. Rosner:] The only relatively consistent
laboratory abnormalities in multiple sclerosis

00:15:44.500 --> 00:15:46.740
are spinal fluid changes.

00:15:47.560 --> 00:15:50.480
The spinal fluid may be entirely normal.

00:15:50.520 --> 00:15:56.000
This occurred in 40 percent of patients in
the UCLA Multiple Sclerosis Clinic.

00:15:56.000 --> 00:16:02.140
An elevated gamma globulin content, over 13 percent of the total protein, was found in 58 percent.

00:16:04.240 --> 00:16:10.540
The colloidal gold curve was abnormal, the
numbers adding up to ten or more in 36 percent.

00:16:10.680 --> 00:16:15.260
This test is an indirect measure of relative
gamma globulin elevation.

00:16:15.420 --> 00:16:21.880
There was an elevated protein in 35 percent,
an increased white cell count in 20 percent.

00:16:23.020 --> 00:16:28.700
With no pathognomonic laboratory test by which
to confirm the diagnosis,

00:16:29.460 --> 00:16:33.340
the doctor must rely on his evaluation of the history and the physical examination.

00:16:35.100 --> 00:16:39.460
The clinical criteria for the diagnosis of
multiple sclerosis are two.

00:16:39.620 --> 00:16:42.440
Number one, episodic course.

00:16:42.720 --> 00:16:50.160
Number two, multiple symptoms and signs pointing
to optic nerve, brain stem, or spinal cord.

00:16:50.800 --> 00:16:56.400
Optic nerve manifestations are: decreased
visual acuity, central scotoma,

00:16:56.420 --> 00:17:01.200
or paracentral, cecocentral, or peripheral
on visual field examination

00:17:01.380 --> 00:17:05.260
and optic atrophy on ophthalmoscopic examination.

00:17:05.660 --> 00:17:12.040
Brain stem manifestations include nystagmus,
the disconjugate gaze difficulty known as

00:17:12.040 --> 00:17:18.280
internuclear ophthalmoplegia, trigeminal neuralgia,
facial sensory deficit, facial weakness,

00:17:18.280 --> 00:17:26.440
vertigo, dysarthria, dysphagia, emotional
lability, and ataxia of the head, trunk, or limbs.

00:17:26.760 --> 00:17:32.680
Spinal cord manifestations consist of the
electric sensations on flexing the neck

00:17:32.680 --> 00:17:38.960
known as Lhermitte's sign, tight band feelings
around the trunk called girdle sensations,

00:17:39.260 --> 00:17:46.480
superficial or proprioceptor sensory deficit,
spastic weakness with hyperactive and pathological reflexes,

00:17:46.940 --> 00:17:49.780
and neurogenic bladder disorder.

00:17:51.220 --> 00:17:57.440
Variations in the course and in the signs
define four varieties of multiple sclerosis,

00:17:57.660 --> 00:18:00.440
the incidence of which is as follows.

00:18:01.040 --> 00:18:07.180
Number one, episodic disseminated, the classical
type, 78 percent.

00:18:07.640 --> 00:18:11.360
Number two, progressive disseminated, 15 percent.

00:18:11.900 --> 00:18:16.140
Number three, episodic non-disseminated, five
percent.

00:18:16.520 --> 00:18:20.200
Number four, progressive non-disseminated,
two percent.

00:18:20.800 --> 00:18:25.040
Returning to our five patients, it will be
seen that the first three represent

00:18:25.140 --> 00:18:27.860
the classical type of multiple sclerosis.

00:18:28.000 --> 00:18:30.440
The other two, atypical types.

00:18:36.320 --> 00:18:40.860
The college student in the first year of her
illness had intermittent sensory symptoms

00:18:40.860 --> 00:18:42.760
with no objective signs.

00:18:42.920 --> 00:18:45.780
She was considered neurotic at that time.

00:18:46.020 --> 00:18:52.140
Many patients in the early stages of multiple
sclerosis are given the diagnosis of psychoneurosis.

00:18:52.460 --> 00:18:54.820
The differential can be a difficult one.

00:18:54.820 --> 00:18:58.880
It is recommended that multiple sclerosis
be diagnosed only if there are

00:18:58.880 --> 00:19:02.700
documented, objective abnormalities on examination.

00:19:03.240 --> 00:19:09.040
When this young lady developed the scotomas
of optic neuritis and the Lhermitte's sign

00:19:09.040 --> 00:19:14.020
of spinal cord involvement, there was objective
evidence of neurological disease

00:19:14.020 --> 00:19:16.960
and definite evidence of dissemination.

00:19:17.220 --> 00:19:22.080
The spinal fluid was normal, except for an
elevated gamma globulin of 20 percent.

00:19:22.380 --> 00:19:25.940
Then the diagnosis of multiple sclerosis could
be made.

00:19:26.180 --> 00:19:30.040
The excellent remission further confirmed
this impression.

00:19:34.700 --> 00:19:39.030
The sales manager began with an attack suggesting
both brain stem

00:19:39.030 --> 00:19:41.440
and spinal cord pathology.

00:19:41.600 --> 00:19:45.940
With complete remission of these symptoms,
multiple sclerosis was suspected,

00:19:46.000 --> 00:19:50.880
but other remitting conditions occurring at
the cervicomedullary junction region

00:19:51.000 --> 00:19:52.440
were still possible.

00:19:52.720 --> 00:19:58.640
After a two-year interval, he developed the
disconjugate gaze difficulty of brain stem disease

00:19:58.960 --> 00:20:01.800
and the spinal cord sign of Lhermitte.

00:20:02.220 --> 00:20:08.180
Now, the diagnosis of multiple sclerosis was
definite on the basis of episodic course

00:20:08.180 --> 00:20:10.260
and disseminated signs.

00:20:10.520 --> 00:20:14.480
A normal spinal fluid reinforced this conclusion.

00:20:20.260 --> 00:20:25.400
The pretty young clerk had only brain stem
manifestations with her first attack.

00:20:25.800 --> 00:20:30.800
Multiple sclerosis could not be diagnosed
at that time, as several other diseases

00:20:30.800 --> 00:20:33.240
can give a similar picture with remission.

00:20:33.240 --> 00:20:36.960
For example, cholesteatoma in the posterior
fossa.

00:20:37.500 --> 00:20:42.340
In the second attack, there were sensory symptoms
suggestive of spinal cord involvement

00:20:42.420 --> 00:20:45.520
in addition to the previous brain stem signs.

00:20:45.680 --> 00:20:50.060
There was still the possibility of a compressive
lesion at the foramen magnum.

00:20:50.680 --> 00:20:54.880
Only with her third attack, when signs of
optic neuritis occurred,

00:20:55.000 --> 00:20:57.420
was dissemination unequivocal.

00:20:57.760 --> 00:21:03.400
The diagnosis could not be made with assurance
then, until this, the third year of her illness.

00:21:08.960 --> 00:21:13.000
The housewife has had a progressive, non-remitting
course.

00:21:13.300 --> 00:21:18.280
This occurs in ten to 40 percent of MS patients
in different large series.

00:21:18.900 --> 00:21:24.760
It is more common with an older age of onset
and with a spinal cord type of onset.

00:21:25.500 --> 00:21:30.780
With time, it became apparent that this lady
had damage in both the brain stem and spinal cord,

00:21:31.140 --> 00:21:37.940
as evidenced by the nystagmus and ataxia on the one hand and the spastic paraparesis on the other.

00:21:38.400 --> 00:21:43.860
The further development of bilateral internuclear
ophthalmoplegia confirms the diagnosis

00:21:43.860 --> 00:21:45.660
of multiple sclerosis.

00:21:51.320 --> 00:21:55.840
The schoolteacher initially had only nystagmus,
which remitted.

00:21:56.000 --> 00:21:59.800
After a one-year interval, intermittent ataxia
appeared.

00:22:00.100 --> 00:22:06.120
Subsequently, the ataxia became constant,
and he developed a spastic left hemiparesis

00:22:06.120 --> 00:22:10.860
with bilateral hyperreflexia and pathological reflexes.

00:22:11.060 --> 00:22:14.520
All signs could be localized to the brain stem.

00:22:14.920 --> 00:22:19.180
The early remissions suggested multiple sclerosis,
but the absence of

00:22:19.360 --> 00:22:24.860
signs of dissemination necessitated the performance
of many special tests.

00:22:25.080 --> 00:22:29.680
The entirely normal spinal fluid was further
evidence of multiple sclerosis.

00:22:29.920 --> 00:22:36.180
However, in this type of case, the doctor
should be especially cautious in his diagnosis.

00:22:37.720 --> 00:22:40.060
After the diagnosis, then what?

00:22:41.200 --> 00:22:45.300
Although multiple sclerosis has been known for almost 100 years,

00:22:45.420 --> 00:22:47.520
its etiology and its treatment

00:22:47.700 --> 00:22:49.240
are still unsettled.

00:22:50.480 --> 00:22:54.180
One important clue is the epidemiology of
the disease.

00:22:54.440 --> 00:22:58.670
The geographical distribution is that of a
low prevalence in tropical zones

00:22:58.670 --> 00:23:03.760
and a high prevalence in temperate and northern
zones where studies have been made.

00:23:05.120 --> 00:23:09.760
Certain factors commonly found to precipitate
exacerbations of the disease include

00:23:09.760 --> 00:23:14.160
physical exhaustion, infection, surgical procedures,
and emotional crises.

00:23:14.320 --> 00:23:19.800
This patient's most recent exacerbation was
in association with an emotional crisis.

00:23:20.900 --> 00:23:24.920
When an attack occurs, bed rest at the beginning
may decrease the duration

00:23:25.080 --> 00:23:27.020
and the severity of the relapse.

00:23:27.260 --> 00:23:31.640
Symptomatic treatment includes the use of
anti-vertigo drugs, muscle relaxants,

00:23:31.720 --> 00:23:35.280
antispasmodics for the bladder, and physical
therapy.

00:23:35.560 --> 00:23:40.300
Most important of all is the psychological
support that the doctor can render the patient

00:23:40.580 --> 00:23:43.640
by giving him attention, encouragement, and
hope.

00:23:45.260 --> 00:23:49.760
Specific treatment for multiple sclerosis
must await the discovery of the cause.

00:23:50.020 --> 00:23:53.320
Many theories have been proposed, but none
has been proved.

00:23:53.540 --> 00:23:59.040
Research programs are now studying the problems
of precipitants in the exacerbations of MS:

00:23:59.320 --> 00:24:05.520
geographical factors in its incidence, the
nature and function of myelin, the significance of

00:24:05.680 --> 00:24:11.220
anti-myelin antibodies, and the experimental
demyelinating disease of animals.

00:24:11.660 --> 00:24:16.980
The solution to multiple sclerosis will open
the door to an understanding

00:24:17.080 --> 00:24:19.880
of many other neurological problems.

00:24:21.420 --> 00:24:27.320
Speaking for the National Multiple Sclerosis
Society is Dr. Augustus S. Rose,

00:24:27.320 --> 00:24:31.540
Professor of Neurology at the University of
California, Los Angeles.

00:24:33.580 --> 00:24:37.640
[Dr. Augustus S. Rose:] It is generally believed
that patients derive encouragement and hope

00:24:37.640 --> 00:24:41.560
through the effort and programs of the National
Multiple Sclerosis Society.

00:24:42.080 --> 00:24:47.960
Not many years ago, there was comparatively
little scientific and public interest

00:24:47.960 --> 00:24:50.200
in the problem of multiple sclerosis.

00:24:51.160 --> 00:24:58.040
Today, it is recognized as the leading neurological
disorder of our time and a major health problem.

00:24:58.580 --> 00:25:04.540
A large and diversified research program is
being conducted in many laboratories throughout

00:25:04.540 --> 00:25:07.480
the world and with promising results.

00:25:08.280 --> 00:25:13.160
Through research and research fellowship training grants, the National Multiple Sclerosis Society

00:25:13.300 --> 00:25:18.980
supports fundamental, applied, and clinical
studies considered to have relationship

00:25:18.980 --> 00:25:22.460
to the problem of multiple sclerosis and demyelination.

00:25:23.140 --> 00:25:30.080
Physicians and research persons at a postdoctoral
level interested in these programs

00:25:30.360 --> 00:25:35.300
should communicate with the medical and research director of the National Multiple Sclerosis Society

00:25:35.620 --> 00:25:37.120
in New York City.

